			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Remove redundant ApplicationState re-exports\n\nEliminate the explicit `pub use ApplicationState::*` statement and extra blank lines in `Source/ApplicationState/State/mod.rs`. The module already imports the types directly via `pub mod ApplicationState;`, making the wildcard re-export unnecessary and redundant for backward compatibility.\n\nThis simplification cleans up the module namespace, adheres to Rust idioms by avoiding redundant re-exports, and reduces potential confusion regarding symbol visibility in the core `ApplicationState` container.",
			"SHA": "d820a1af5b83b56f9655d169290065485006f751"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-02T06:34:04Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1109,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Add UUID generator for Air request correlation\n\nIntroduce `GenerateRequestID.rs` in the `AirServiceProvider` module to generate fresh UUID-v4 identifiers for Air RPC requests. Each request now carries a unique ID, enabling Mountain to correlate replies with originating calls across logs and traces during communication with the Air daemon sidecar.\n\nThis utility supports the upcoming Air integration contract defined in the `AirServiceTypesStub`, ensuring request/response matching for update, metrics, and file indexing operations. The implementation uses the `uuid` crate with the simple format and adheres to PascalCase naming for the function `Fn`.",
			"SHA": "e3df3b7142bc02b017b24d730fc95201b735dc5a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-02T06:33:59Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1107,
				3
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Implement debug adapter lifecycle RPC handlers\n\nIntroduce three new gRPC handlers in the CocoonService debug module to fulfill the Vine protocol contract for debugging support. Implement `RegisterDebugAdapter` to register debug types in ApplicationState and emit `sky://debug/register` events to activate the launch UI. Add `StartDebugging` to mint session IDs and broadcast `sky://debug/start` events with configuration details, and `StopDebugging` to emit `sky://debug/sessionEnd` notifications upon termination.\n\nThese handlers bridge the extension host (Cocoon) with the Sky frontend, enabling the full debug lifecycle: registration of debug adapters, session initiation with proper context, and graceful session teardown. This completes the IPC contract required for VS Code extension debugging support within the Land editor.",
			"SHA": "4fb2a4f6a0d727fc8c1de5f525b9e7d366f17562"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-02T06:33:50Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1103,
				4
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Standardize function signatures and resolve Rust clippy lints\n\nAddress formatting inconsistencies and clippy warnings across the `WindServiceHandlers` module and the main IPC dispatcher. Standardize multi-line function signature formatting to ensure the `Result` type appears on the same line as the signature where possible, and align parameter lists for readability.\n\nUpdate internal dispatch calls in `mountain_ipc_invoke` to use explicit `.Fn` syntax for `WaitForClientConnection`, `SendRequest`, and `SendNotification` methods, resolving method resolution ambiguity. Adjust import grouping in `mod.rs` and fix spacing around variable declarations to comply with Rust formatting standards.\n\nThese changes improve code consistency and ensure the build passes without clippy warnings while maintaining functional parity for configuration, extension, and search IPC handlers.",
			"SHA": "d2cf6dccc0fe0dfc95e50ced5c54ee90efcfd7c2"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-02T06:33:41Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1103,
				20
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Stub Air client and DTOs for update/metrics IPC contract\n\nIntroduce a complete set of stub types and a placeholder client implementation for the Air daemon sidecar in `Source/Air/AirServiceTypesStub`. This prepares the `Vine` protocol contract for background services including update management, file indexing, authentication, and metrics collection.\n\nThe new module defines request and response DTOs for operations like `CheckForUpdates`, `DownloadFile`, `IndexFiles`, and `GetMetrics`, adhering to the project's PascalCase naming convention. The `AirClientType` struct provides a feature-flagged stub implementation that returns a descriptive error when the `AirIntegration` feature is disabled, allowing the build to proceed without the actual daemon link.\n\nThis scaffolding enables the definition of gRPC contracts and type safety between Mountain and the future Air sidecar before the integration logic is implemented.",
			"SHA": "27ceae2065f32f43709f6bf8d14e7ddabe008e57"
		}
	],
